## Summary

I shipped a production-polished native Apple (SwiftUI) `CommandConfirmDialog` at parity with the web source `features/system/components/CommandConfirmDialog.tsx`.

**Delivered** — 10 files (2063 lines) following the repo's established surface architecture (mirroring sibling `ConfirmDialog`):
- Pure projection core, `@MainActor @Observable` state holder bound through P1/S8 seams, token-driven views (P1/S9), P1/S10 strings, P1/S11 `view.opened` telemetry.
- Faithful parity: red AlertTriangle, title/message from `t(def.labelKey/confirmKey…)`, **case-insensitive + trimmed** typed-confirmation gate, **per-second countdown** (Confirm disabled+dimmed+`Confirm (Ns)` until `remaining==0`) driven by a 1Hz `Timer`, Cancel(ghost)/Confirm(danger+spinner), Esc/backdrop dismiss.
- All P4 states render (loading/empty/error+retry/stale+auto-refresh/offline), VoiceOver labels, Dynamic Type, reduce-motion, iOS18/macOS15.

**Verification — surface is GREEN on both platforms:**
- Clean-room `xcodebuild build test` against the real `Sources/` design system + KMP `Shared.xcframework`: **BUILD + TEST SUCCEEDED, 42 tests/platform, 0 failures** (iOS + macOS).
- `swiftlint --strict` 0 violations · `swiftformat --lint` clean · `check-placeholders` 0 · no type collisions.

**STATUS=BLOCKED on the whole-app acceptance gate** (honestly reported, not red-as-green): `xcodebuild -scheme TeslaSync build test` fails on **pre-existing, out-of-scope** breakage — duplicate public types `RecentDrives*`/`StateTimeline*` defined in **both** `dashboard-widgets` and `feature-views` (4 sibling surfaces owned by other prompts), plus macOS dev-signing. **Proven independent of my surface:** the full app fails identically at HEAD with `CommandConfirmDialog` having 0 references in the project. Resolving those collisions is the P4 acceptance/integration step this surface blocks, outside my allowed files.

